zreader 0.6.0 / priority features 1-5 / BOX-TESTED, NOT DEPLOYED

Completed, in the requested priority order
1. Per-book PDF fit-page, auto-cropped fit-width / 96px-overlap screen slices,
   1.5x/2x double-tap zoom, bounded one-finger pan on release, current-view
   worker prefetch and persistent mode/slice/pan/base state. Cropped width is
   retained in zoom even with the independent Trim toggle off. No pinch.
2. EPUB chapter/Unicode-scalar anchors + chapter checksum for persistent reading
   targets and notes. No opaque pointer bookmarks on disk. Migrate legacy notes
   in their OLD CSS/layout before new typography; use quote + old quad to choose
   the exact repeated occurrence. Resolve highlights into current layout quads,
   including across multiple newly laid-out pages. Nine 14-40 CSS-px equivalent
   font sizes, 3 line-height settings and adjustable margins. Exact quarter-point
   font persistence and stable within-page target prevent cumulative drift.
   Fixed legacy JSON \u decoding, including surrogate pairs and UTF-8 validation.
   Unresolved notes remain visible in Notes/exports, but never mark random text.
3. Offline English WordNet dictionary. Long-press one word, Define; paginated
   full senses panel, simple inflection/possessive/irregular/accent fallbacks.
   Sorted keys/shared offsets, bounds-checked read-only mmap, no network/runtime
   dependencies. Missing/corrupt dictionary gives a safe actionable panel.
4. Menu Search, big-key English keyboard, native MuPDF case-insensitive matching,
   snippets/page numbers, incremental/cancellable per-page scan. Up to 200 hits;
   tap preserves view and scrolls/pans to target; temporary 1.6s hit mark clears
   without creating an annotation. No OCR / cross-page-phrase matching.
5. Markdown rewritten on every note mutation at DATA/export/<book>.md, including
   deletes and copies. Export all handles unopened books, escapes markup and
   skips symlinks; corrupt input is reported, not rewritten into source notes.

Deliberately deferred (no incomplete hardware features shipped)
6. New library thumbnail cache/folder navigation/additional sorts/progress bars.
   Existing recursive library and recent-book behavior remain.
7. Reader-managed sleep/wake/suspend/cover sleep screen. Power still exits to
   Amazon UI. No powerd suspend or /sys/power/state write was added.
8. Frontlight/warmth sliders and restore. No new light or warmth control runs.

Core-dump suppression preparation
- Opt-in zreader-maintenance.sh with status / disable-core-dumps /
  undo-core-dumps; optional ZREADER_DISABLE_CORE_DUMPS=1 launcher hook, default
  OFF. It creates only an empty /mnt/us/DISABLE_CORE_DUMP and an ownership receipt.
- Undo removes only the still-empty regular marker with matching inode/device.
  Existing, nonempty, replaced or symlink markers are preserved. No dumps deleted.
  Inode changes across remount/reboot can make undo refuse; inspect manually.
- Exact commands / undo / risks in README. No change was applied to any device.
- Public MIP wiki and MobileRead reports recommend this firmware sentinel for
  KPPMainApp/KPPMainAppV2 and Mesquite. Exact PW6 firmware core_pattern/handler /
  upstart implementation has NOT been inspected, so efficacy is unverified.
  No rootfs/upstart/core_pattern/jailbreak setting was modified; ulimit in this
  shell could not disable dumps from an already-running Amazon daemon anyway.
- Sources: https://mip-wiki.pages.dev/database/crashlog/
  https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=366779
  https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=365536

